WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.559
Week ten.

00:00:01.609 --> 00:00:06.747
Inside the world of influencer marketing, with Bryce Coombe, managing director of Hypetap.

00:00:06.797 --> 00:00:10.618
His message: influencer is no longer a side channel.

00:00:11.333 --> 00:00:15.764
Hypetap is a full service influencer agency, founded in twenty fourteen.

00:00:15.814 --> 00:00:20.827
It calls itself more than a platform, running on people, process and product.

00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:24.915
Australia has twenty one point three million social media users,

00:00:24.965 --> 00:00:26.342
each on six or more platforms a month.

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:30.523
And TikTok time is up six hours on last year.

00:00:31.233 --> 00:00:33.836
Guess the average Australian TikTok user.

00:00:33.886 --> 00:00:35.570
She's a thirty nine year old woman,

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:36.420
watching a movie's worth,

00:00:35.985 --> 00:00:38.117
about ninety minutes,

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:39.839
every single night.

00:00:40.533 --> 00:00:41.886
Why does it work?

00:00:41.936 --> 00:00:44.846
Eighty percent are on TikTok mainly for creators.

00:00:44.896 --> 00:00:46.592
Seventy five percent have acted on a product in their feed.

00:00:46.642 --> 00:00:51.947
And twenty percent use social for inspiration while buying.

00:00:52.633 --> 00:00:54.458
But value is different here.

00:00:54.508 --> 00:00:58.444
A creator's recipe showing cookware in real life gets positive sentiment.

00:00:58.494 --> 00:01:02.199
Strict brand instructions get neutral sentiment at best.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:04.631
Social is now search.

00:01:04.681 --> 00:01:08.227
Nearly half of US consumers use TikTok as a search engine.

00:01:08.277 --> 00:01:13.138
Google indexes creator content, and AI models learn about brands from it.

00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:14.633
So it's not just another channel that interrupts the broadcast.

00:01:14.116 --> 00:01:18.830
It works through peer validation,

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.248
algorithmic trust and cultural resonance,

00:01:21.298 --> 00:01:24.815
which beats standard attention by two hundred and forty six percent.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.207
Know your brand's eye level.

00:01:27.257 --> 00:01:29.271
Leader brands use experts.

00:01:29.321 --> 00:01:32.007
Eye to eye brands use just like you creators.

00:01:32.057 --> 00:01:35.066
Subservient brands do the work for people.

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:38.040
Fast growth attracts opportunists.

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:43.606
Brands that treat creators transactionally, influencers who fake their reach, and agency cowboys.

00:01:43.656 --> 00:01:46.845
His rule: never trust a screen grab.

00:01:47.533 --> 00:01:51.080
The big one: the brand is liable, not the influencer.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:55.195
A free product counts as paid advertising, so it must be disclosed.

00:01:55.245 --> 00:01:59.907
Infringement notices for a listed company reach a hundred and thirty three thousand dollars.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.000
Assets count too.

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:05.951
Music, clips, even a reposted meme can breach copyright.

00:02:06.001 --> 00:02:08.439
Warner Music is suing Crumbl Cookies.

00:02:08.489 --> 00:02:12.254
Rights owners wait for many breaches, then sue big.

00:02:12.967 --> 00:02:16.655
AIMCO's Code of Practice cuts legal risk and wasted spend,

00:02:16.705 --> 00:02:17.505
with clear rules for contracts and reporting.

00:02:17.448 --> 00:02:23.373
For consumers, it means choice, protection and trust.

00:02:24.067 --> 00:02:26.942
Brand safety is deeper than a few thumb scrolls.

00:02:26.992 --> 00:02:30.621
Check deleted posts, fit, swearing and politics.

00:02:30.671 --> 00:02:32.956
Kmart's celebrity pair looked good on paper,

00:02:33.006 --> 00:02:34.194
but audiences said,

00:02:34.244 --> 00:02:36.513
these two don't shop at Kmart.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.464
Finally, measure growth, not just attention.

00:02:40.514 --> 00:02:43.058
Views and engagement explain attention.

00:02:43.108 --> 00:02:44.603
Growth comes from visibility,

00:02:44.653 --> 00:02:45.876
mental availability,

00:02:45.926 --> 00:02:46.973
share of voice,

00:02:47.023 --> 00:02:49.670
brand perception and behaviour change.

00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:51.378
Want in?

00:02:51.428 --> 00:02:52.369
Account management is a good entry point, because it covers everything.

00:02:52.419 --> 00:02:59.165
And bring something extra, or you're lost in a sea of sameness.

00:02:59.867 --> 00:03:02.659
So treat influencer as a specialist discipline.

00:03:02.709 --> 00:03:05.112
Know the brand carries the legal risk.

00:03:05.162 --> 00:03:07.706
And measure growth, not just attention.

00:03:07.756 --> 00:03:09.481
That's week ten.
